<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54486" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ-ᾰμάω</span></b> , once in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> in 
			Med.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>scrape up, heap
			up</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήν ῥα</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν κόπρον</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> κυλινδόμενος καταμήσατο Χερσὶν ἑῇσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.165
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν Χοῦν καταμήσονται</span>
			(Mein. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακοιμήσονται</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				121
			</span></i>: c. gen., <i>heap upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταμώμενοι τῆς κεφαλῆς κόνιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					2.15.4
				</span></i>
			, v.l. ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.21.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ αὖ νιν . . νερτέρων ἀμᾷ
			κοπίς</span> (Jortin for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόνις</span>)
				<i>cuts</i> it <i>down, reaps</i> it <i>like corn</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				601
			</span></i> (lyr.); if <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόνις</span> is
			retained, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταμᾷ</span> must be rendered
				<i>covers over.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
